#	Topic / Issue	Cause & Technical Details	Solution Provided	Code / Config Evidence
1	
Groq Vision Payload Crash


messages[0].content must be a string

You switched your model in Agent 3 to openai/gpt-oss-120b. On Groq, gpt-oss-120b is a text-only model. When base64 image objects were passed inside messages[0].content in _analyze_damage, Groq rejected the structured image-array payload.	Split Agent 3 into a two-step pipeline: use a Vision-capable model for image analysis, and use openai/gpt-oss-120b strictly for the text-only cost estimation.	
Before:


python\n# Sent image array to text-only model\nresponse = groq_client.chat.completions.create(\n model="openai/gpt-oss-120b",\n messages=[{"role": "user", "content": content_with_images}]\n)\n


After:


python\n# Step 1: Vision model for image array\n_analyze_damage(model="qwen/qwen3.6-27b")\n\n# Step 2: Text model for text estimation\n_generate_final_estimate(model="openai/gpt-oss-120b")\n

